<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abraham Duquesne</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1610–<a href="/years/1688">1688</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abraham Duquesne was a French naval commander, a Protestant from Dieppe, who became one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a>'s leading admirals. In 1676 he defeated a Dutch-Spanish fleet under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michiel-de-ruyter">Michiel de Ruyter</a> at the Battle of Augusta off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>. In 1682 and 1683 he bombarded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> with newly developed bomb vessels, destroying much of the lower town and forcing the release of French captives.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abraham-duquesne.jpg" alt="Abraham Duquesne" width="320" height="397" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexander Joseph von Steuben · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marquis_Abraham_Duquesne_(1610-1688).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
